    {
      "_type": "UMLActivity",
      "_id": "2b81ea96a24e45c899793a6b92b580fe",
      "_parent": {
        "$ref": "736ea0c16e384507b465d053f5e02264"
      },
      "name": "AD-10 - Administrative Reporting & Audit",
      "visibility": "public",
      "isAbstract": false,
      "isReadOnly": false,
      "isSingleExecution": false,
      "documentation": "Activity Diagram derived from UC-20 (View Administrative Reports) and UC-21 (View Audit Log).\nShows an Administrator accessing the administrative area, passing authorization, selecting either the Reports function or the Audit Log function, retrieving the relevant information, and reviewing the result.\n\nPreconditions:\n1. The Administrator can access the administrative reporting/audit area.\n2. Report data and/or audit records may or may not currently be available.\n\nPostconditions (success): The requested administrative report or audit records are displayed and reviewed by the Administrator.\nPostconditions (alternative): Access is denied for an unauthorized user, OR report data is unavailable / report generation fails, OR no matching audit records are found / audit-record retrieval fails.\n\nScope boundary: This workflow is read-only. It does not modify users/roles, the medicine catalogue, stock, or price information, and does not perform report resolution (see AD-06 for report review/resolution of incorrect-information reports). No data is fabricated: no-data and failure conditions are shown explicitly rather than substituted with invented records.\n\nDesign note: The source specification (MedAccess_AD10_Administrative_Reporting_and_Audit.md) lists two distinct audit-failure labels ('Display no matching audit events' and 'Display audit-log retrieval failure') but its Main Flow / Compact Flow shows only a single 'Audit records available?' decision with one [No] path. Both labels are preserved by combining them into the single No-branch action, mirroring how the Reports branch already combines 'no data' and 'generation failure' into one 'Report data available / generated successfully?' decision and one combined failure action. This is a deliberate reconciliation of the source document's own internal inconsistency, not an invented requirement.\n\nOptional 'Continue?' loop-back (mentioned as optional in the source spec) is omitted to keep the diagram uncluttered; both the Reports and Audit Log review steps flow to the shared Activity Final Node instead.\n\nTraceability: UC-20 - View Administrative Reports; UC-21 - View Audit Log; FR-35-FR-39.",
      "ownedElements": [
